# Replayable semantic evidence

AshR2RML already has distinct owners for compilation, Reactor orchestration,
SPARQL/OBDA execution, parity, and OCEL telemetry. The useful invariant is not a
new global "session" object. It is that the existing artifacts can be joined by
stable content identity while each subsystem keeps its authority boundary.

This notebook is executable in CI with `mix ash_r2rml.test_livebooks`.
Only cells explicitly marked `ash_r2rml:test` participate in headless testing.

## One query, stable observed identity

<!-- ash_r2rml:test -->
```elixir
import ExUnit.Assertions

knows = RDF.iri("https://example.org/knows")
alice = RDF.iri("https://example.org/alice")
bob = RDF.iri("https://example.org/bob")

graph = RDF.Graph.new([{alice, knows, bob}])

query = """
PREFIX ex: <https://example.org/>
SELECT ?person WHERE { ex:alice ex:knows ?person . }
"""

{:ok, first} = AshR2RML.SPARQL.Local.query(graph, query)
{:ok, replay} = AshR2RML.SPARQL.Local.query(graph, query)

assert first.query_sha256 == replay.query_sha256
assert first.result_sha256 == replay.result_sha256
assert AshR2RML.Evidence.id(first) == AshR2RML.Evidence.id(replay)
assert first.rows == [%{"person" => "https://example.org/bob"}]
```

## OCEL run identity selects a trace; semantic identity survives a new run

OCEL event UUIDs, timestamps, durations, scheduler order, and the Reactor run UUID
are observations of transport. They select and describe an execution, but they
must not make two semantically identical executions look different.

<!-- ash_r2rml:test -->
```elixir
first_execution = "run-first"
replay_execution = "run-replay"

compile = %{
  "ocel:eid" => "event-a",
  "ocel:activity" => "ash_r2rml.reactor.compile_resources",
  "ocel:timestamp" => "2026-08-21T20:00:00Z",
  "ocel:lifecycle" => "stop",
  "ocel:omap" => ["reactor-run:run-first", "Example.Person"],
  "ocel:e2o" => [
    %{"ocel:oid" => "reactor-run:run-first", "ocel:qualifier" => "context"},
    %{"ocel:oid" => "Example.Person", "ocel:qualifier" => "target"}
  ],
  "ocel:vmap" => %{
    "execution_id" => first_execution,
    "result_evidence_id" => "mapping-abc",
    "duration_ms" => 12
  }
}

render = %{
  "ocel:eid" => "event-b",
  "ocel:activity" => "ash_r2rml.reactor.render_r2rml_turtle",
  "ocel:timestamp" => "2026-08-21T20:00:01Z",
  "ocel:lifecycle" => "stop",
  "ocel:omap" => ["reactor-run:run-first", "W3CR2RMLRenderer"],
  "ocel:e2o" => [
    %{"ocel:oid" => "reactor-run:run-first", "ocel:qualifier" => "context"},
    %{"ocel:oid" => "W3CR2RMLRenderer", "ocel:qualifier" => "target"}
  ],
  "ocel:vmap" => %{
    "execution_id" => first_execution,
    "result_evidence_id" => "r2rml-def",
    "duration_ms" => 7
  }
}

{:ok, first_trace} = AshR2RML.Evidence.ocel_trace_id([compile, render], first_execution)

noisy_replay =
  [render, compile]
  |> Enum.map(fn event ->
    event
    |> Map.put("ocel:eid", "replay-#{event["ocel:eid"]}")
    |> Map.put("ocel:timestamp", "2026-08-22T01:00:00Z")
    |> update_in(["ocel:omap"], &Enum.map(&1, fn
      "reactor-run:" <> _ -> "reactor-run:run-replay"
      oid -> oid
    end))
    |> update_in(["ocel:e2o"], &Enum.map(&1, fn relation ->
      case relation["ocel:oid"] do
        "reactor-run:" <> _ -> Map.put(relation, "ocel:oid", "reactor-run:run-replay")
        _ -> relation
      end
    end))
    |> put_in(["ocel:vmap", "execution_id"], replay_execution)
    |> put_in(["ocel:vmap", "duration_ms"], 900)
  end)

{:ok, replay_trace} = AshR2RML.Evidence.ocel_trace_id(noisy_replay, replay_execution)
assert first_trace == replay_trace
```

A passing notebook proves only these public deterministic contracts. It does not
manufacture PostgreSQL, remote SPARQL, Ontop, or cutover evidence.
